{{define "content"}}<article class="help-page">
<h1>Help</h1>

<section id="getting-started">
<h2>Getting Started</h2>
<p>Shorten a URL with a single request — no API key required:</p>
<pre><code>curl -X POST {{.Base.SiteName}}/api/v1/links \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"url":"https://example.com/very/long/path"}'</code></pre>
<p>Response:</p>
<pre><code>{
  "short_code": "aZ3kQ1",
  "short_url": "https://example.com/aZ3kQ1",
  "destination_url": "https://example.com/very/long/path",
  "owner_token": "tok_...",
  "created_at": "2026-08-07T00:00:00Z"
}</code></pre>
<p>Save the <code>owner_token</code> — it authorizes later edits or deletion of that
link and is shown only once.</p>
</section>

<section id="features">
<h2>Features</h2>

<h3>Custom slugs</h3>
<p>Request a specific short code instead of an auto-generated one:</p>
<pre><code>curl -X POST {{.Base.SiteName}}/api/v1/links \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"url":"https://example.com","slug":"my-link"}'</code></pre>
<p>Slugs must be 3-20 characters, letters/numbers/hyphens, and cannot collide
with a reserved system name (e.g. <code>api</code>, <code>server</code>,
<code>static</code>, <code>about</code>).</p>

<h3>Managing a link</h3>
<p>Update or delete a link using the <code>owner_token</code> from creation:</p>
<pre><code>curl -X PATCH {{.Base.SiteName}}/api/v1/links/my-link \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer tok_..." \
  -d '{"destination_url":"https://example.com/new-path"}'

curl -X DELETE {{.Base.SiteName}}/api/v1/links/my-link \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer tok_..."</code></pre>

<h3>Click analytics</h3>
<p>Every link has a stats page — visit it in a browser, or fetch it as JSON:</p>
<pre><code>curl {{.Base.SiteName}}/my-link/stats -H "Accept: application/json"</code></pre>
<p>Visitor IP addresses are anonymized before being stored, so stats show
aggregate traffic without exposing individual visitors.</p>
</section>

<div class="api-docs">
<h3>API Documentation</h3>
<p>This application provides a full REST API. See the API reference for the
complete endpoint list and request/response formats.</p>
</div>

