<section id="faq">
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Do I need an account?</h3>
<p>No. Anyone can create a short link anonymously; the response's
<code>owner_token</code> is your only credential for managing that link.</p>
<h3>Is there a rate limit?</h3>
<p>Yes — anonymous link creation is rate-limited per IP address to prevent abuse.</p>
<h3>What happens to expired links?</h3>
<p>A resolve request for an expired link returns <code>410 Gone</code> instead of redirecting.</p>
</section>

<section id="troubleshooting">
<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
<h3>404 on a short link</h3>
<p>The link doesn't exist, was deleted, or the slug was mistyped.</p>
<h3>410 Gone</h3>
<p>The link existed but has expired.</p>
<h3>409 Conflict when creating a custom slug</h3>
<p>That slug is already taken or is a reserved system name — choose another.</p>
</section>
